		"category": Category.MEDICAL,
		"severity": 4,
		"danger": 5,
		"scale": 1,
		"type": Category.MEDICAL,
		"description": "Vacuum Exposure is a common Medical incident that can occur on the surface of the Moon. While all Airlocks and Suits are equipped with top-of-the-line Anti-Vacuum technology, accidents and tampering can still occur. Typically, Vacuum Exposure presents itself with the following symptoms; Sudden Asphyxiation, Ebullism (Boiling of the soft tissue), Swelling, and burns. Due to this, Vacuum Exposures are typically called in by an individual recovering someone who has. \n \n However, long term effects of Vacuum Exposure have been noted, such as Difficultly Breathing, High Blood Pressure, Anxiety around Airlocks, and Nightmares.",
