		"severity": 2,
		"danger": 2,
		"scale": 1,
		"type": Category.GENERAL,
		"description": "Airlock Malfunctions are a dangerous type of malfunction that can affect Airlocks. However, this designation is a general field for a variety of malfunctions that can take place within an Airlock. These malfunctions are, [REMOVED FOR THE SAKE OF BREVITY]. However, due to the likely emergent status an Operator will find themselves when reporting a Airlock Malfunction, it is best to diagnose a Airlock Malfunction by it's effects on people, which are typically the following; Loss of Breath, Headaches, Migranes, Crushed Limbs, Crushed Fingers, Misidentification of Personnel, and Paranoia ",
