	},
	{
		"id": 69,
		"name": "Pollen Burst",
		"category": Category.ANOMALOUS,
		"severity": 3,
		"danger": 3,
		"scale": 4,
		"type": Category.BIOLOGICAL,
		"description": "Pollen Bursts are a geyser-like Biological Anomaly that commonly occurs in regions of the Moon above large cave systems which sends tons of unknown pollen into the space above an instance. That said, most Pollen Bursts occur below Outposts, which leads to the pollen infiltrating the ventilation system. This is where reporting a Pollen Burst becomes tricky. Pollen Infection comes in 3 stages. \n \n If you believe that nobody is showing signs of Pollen Infection, such as Fever, Headache, Lack of Mobility, Bone Aches, Sneezing, Watery Eyes, Coughing, Teethache, or Tiredness, Please report as a Pollen Burst. If anyone related to the call is displaying these symptoms, please report as a Pollen Infection (#76). If the caller reports a previous Pollen Burst or Infection, and is now reporting remnants of grass, flowers, or similar natural plants, or a creature made out of them, please report as a Geminite (#92)",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 2,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 70,
		"name": "Lab Suite Instability",
		"category": Category.SCIENTIFIC,
		"severity": 5,
		"danger": 1,
		"scale": 2,
		"type": Category.SCIENTIFIC,
		"description": "Lab Suite Instability is a common Scientific anomaly that can occur in Lab Suites that are not properly maintained by the proper authorities. L.S.I commonly presents itself as a degradation of the systems involved in the proper function of the lab. Due to this, the degrading systems involved change from call to call. One universal sign of Instability, though, is a weaken connection between the Lab and the wider Lunar Research Database. This can also present itself during the call as literal degradation of the call's quality. Do not confuse this with actually low call quality, which is not handled by M.A.R.S, and instead by the Lunar Telecommunication Authority. ",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 2,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 71,
		"name": "Misplaced Call",
		"category": Category.GENERAL,
		"severity": 1,
		"danger": 1,
		"scale": 1,
		"type": Category.GENERAL,
		"description": "Occasionally, due to the variety of hotline numbers there are reachable by Lunar Dialed Phones, personnel on the surface accidentally call M.A.R.S when they mean to call another number. When this happens, please open the Re-Direct Interface on your Crater and re-dial them to the Lunar Hotline Directory Number, unless you believe that the problem they have is related to M.A.R.S. In that case, please attempt to diagnose the anomaly in question. \n \n If you believe that the call is done under duress, please file as a Duress Call (#72).",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 2,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 72,
		"name": "Duress Calls",
		"category": Category.SECURITY,
		"severity": 3,
		"danger": 3,
		"scale": 1,
		"type": Category.SECURITY,
		"description": "Duress Calls are a type of Security Incident that revolves around calls, both properly placed, and misplaced, to M.A.R.S that the operator believes to be made under the Duress of another party. Most operators casually refer to them as 'Pizza Calls', due to a similar case of a Duress Call on Earth. Duress Calls are primarily identified through the tone and voice of the caller in question, with the typical Duress Caller sounding afraid, sad, hesitant, or quiet. Normally, Duress Callers do not report actual anomalies, and instead report fake anomalies that attempt to pass information about their location and status to the Operator. \n \n If you believe you have received a Duress Call, please use the Lunar Hotline Directory on your C.R.A.T.E.R to patch in the Lunar Security Authority into the call. If you have reason to believe that the individual causing the Duress situation is a part of the security force, please dial the Head of Security themself.",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 3,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 73,
		"name": "Chemical Phantasia",
		"category": Category.SCIENTIFIC,
		"severity": 3,
		"danger": 4,
		"scale": 3,
		"type": Category.ANOMALOUS,
		"description": "Chemical Phantasia is a Scientific anomaly that can occur in labs and storage facilities that primarily house chemicals, or factories that primarily handle chemicals as a part of their production process, which causes the individual affected to imagine the effects of being exposed to a nearby chemical. While, historically, Chemical Phantasia was not a high-presence anomaly, a recent shift towards lunar chemical manufacturing has led to a rise in Chemical Phantasia. Because of this, it is important to note which factory the caller is calling from, and if any incidents regarding chemicals have been reported there. \n \n Because of this, it is recommended that when you suspect a case of Chemical Phantasia, to use the Industrial Accident Database to ensure if any incidents revolving chemicals have been reported. The additional notes section of you Call Interface should also possess information about the location of the caller.",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 1,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 74,
		"name": "Coat",
		"category": Category.ANOMALOUS,
		"severity": 2,
		"danger": 2,
		"scale": 5,
		"type": Category.BIOLOGICAL,
		"description": "Coats are a type of biological organism that has evolved on the Moon. This designation is for the most common species of Coats (Colonia obscurans), which appears as a grimy, dirty coating on surfaces within stations, outposts, and other such structures on the Lunar Surface. \n \n Unlike many lunar organisms, the Coat and it's other species are incredibly difficult to get rid of, primarily due to their enhanced photosynthesis capabilities which makes it incredibly hard to starve. \n \n It is recommended that stations dealing with a Coat close all windows in order to starve out the bacteria, and temporarily seek housing elsewhere in order to prevent it from consuming crumbs from food. \n \n If the Coat does other things, such as heating or cooling down the room it is in, feeding off of other sources besides crumbs and photosynthesis, or any other anomalous effect, please seek out another Coat entry.",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 3,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 75,
		"name": "Class-1 Crime",
		"category": Category.SECURITY,
		"severity": 2,
		"danger": 2,
		"scale": 2,
		"type": Category.SECURITY,
		"description": "A Class-1 Crime is a general designation for crimes that do not harm individuals directly, unlike Class-3 crimes, such as murder, kidnapping, Grand Theft Auto, and more. Historically, when the first Lunar outposts were established, Class-1 crimes were referred to as Misdemeanors. The list of Class-1 crimes is as follows: Reckless Driving, Driving Under Influence (If no death is involved), Speeding, Petty Theft (Below 500 LCs), Shoplifting (Below 500 LCs), Vandalism, Trespassing (In non-restricted but still private places), Possession of Stolen Property, Public Intoxication, Public urination, Possession of under 5 grams of any controlled substances, Stalking, Assault with no weapon and minor injury, Verbal Harassment, Non-violent resisting arrest, and Prostitution.    ",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 1,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 76,
		"name": "Pollen Infection",
		"category": Category.BIOLOGICAL,
		"severity": 3,
		"danger": 3,
		"scale": 5,
		"type": Category.ANOMALOUS,
		"description": "Pollen Infections are a anomalous infection that occurs when an biological organism is exposed to the Pollen from a Pollen Burst (#69). Once exposed to the pollen, a Human individual will start to present with the standard symptoms within 24 to 48 hours, though cases of asymptomatic infection have been noted, but rare. Most people present with the following symptoms; Fever, Headache, Lack of Mobility, Bone Aches, Sneezing, Watery Eyes, Coughing, Teethache, or Tiredness. \n \n If the Pollen has infected an animal, please dispose of the animal, and file as a Geminite (#92). If the Station, Outpost, or other Lunar Building/Ship dealing with a Pollen Infection has a Organic Mainframe or Biological Life Support, please abandon the site in question and file as a Geminite Cluster (#99).",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 4,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 77,
		"name": "Unknown Injury",
		"category": Category.MEDICAL,
		"severity": 3,
		"danger": 3,
		"scale": 1,
		"type": Category.MEDICAL,
		"description": "Unknown Injuries are Injuries with an unknown cause, or symptoms. Unknown Injuries are filed when the caller does not accurately understand the injury they have, or cannot verbalize what the injury entirely is. This is not to be confused the circumstances behind a Duress Call, which is when the caller cannot verbalize the nature of the injuries due to a third party. \n \n While Unknown Injuries are a daily occurrence when humans encounter anomalous phenomenon, M.A.R.S operators are to file based on the primary anomaly at hand, and not any sub-anomalies generated by the actions of the primary. This means, if an individual is calling about an injury caused by another anomaly, you are to file based on the other anomaly first, if possible.  ",
		"icon_path": " ",
		"unlocked_on_day": 2,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 78,
		"name": "Staffing Request",
		"category": Category.GENERAL,
		"severity": 1,
		"danger": 1,
		"scale": 1,
		"type": Category.GENERAL,
		"description": "Staffing Requests refers to calls placed through M.A.R.S requesting for more staff to be sent to a specific location on the Lunar Surface. Due to the nature of these calls, M.A.R.S Operators must bear additional responsibility for the assignment of new staff to fulfill the request, which is done through the Employment Register on their C.R.A.T.E.R. The employees assigned to a Staffing Request call must align with the request of the caller, and Operators will be docked pay for incorrect assignments \n \n If the same caller appears twice in one week requesting staff, please file as a Greater Mimic (#122)",
		"icon_path": " ",
