	{
		"id": 86,
		"name": "Meteor Storm",
		"category": Category.GENERAL,
		"severity": 3,
		"danger": 3,
		"scale": 4,
		"type": Category.SCIENTIFIC,
		"description": "Meteor Storms are a astronomical phenomenon that commonly happens around the Moon due to its gravitational pull and lack of atmosphere. Like Meteor Storms on Earth, this phenomenon involves interplanetary, if not, interstellar rocks crashing down onto the surface of the Moon, however, unlike Earth, due to the lack of an atmosphere, they impact the surface at full force, which can cause damage to the surface and to surrounding structures that aren't properly protected against them. \n \n Meteor Storms are rare, but this entry has been re-introduced back into the M.A.R.S Database due to the Solar Systems entry into a region of the Milky Way with a higher density of rouge Meteors. Most Individuals will report a Meteor Storm as a series of loud impacts and damage to their station, outpost, and etc. ",
