	{
		"id": 89,
		"name": "Moon Sprites",
		"category": Category.BIOLOGICAL,
		"severity": 5,
		"danger": 4,
		"scale": 3,
		"type": Category.ANOMALOUS,
		"description": "Moon Sprites are an unknown biological entity that inhabits several regions of the Moon, which are together known as the Regolith Flats. Sprites are generally thought to be collections of loose energy, such as that from the sun, heat, and loose wiring, that manages to gain form from solidified clumps of regolith, which is what gives Moon Sprites their shape. \n \n The shape and size that Moon Sprites take upon formation are incredibly varied, ranging from small thumb-sized squares to large rover sized orbs. \n \n In order to maintain their shape and continued existence, Moon Sprites must consistently intake energy, either through an unknown from of Photosynthesis, which is more commonly seen in outdoor, large Sprites, or via siphoning power from stations that small sprites inhabit. Because of this, those with indoor sprites commonly report losing power or functionality in certain parts of their station. \n \n It has been rarely reported that larger Sprites attempt to siphon power from stations, though, it is theorized that if they did, the power would lose all functionality completely, including loss of life support.",
