		"danger": 3,
		"scale": 2,
		"type": Category.GEOLOGICAL,
		"description": "Sinkholes are a geological phenomenon that can occur in geologically unstable areas of the moon and involve the rapid implosion of both surface and crust in on itself, causing what is commonly referred to as a sinkhole, though its official lunar variant designation has yet to be decided on. \n \n Like Earth Sinkholes, Lunar Sinkholes pose similar yet very different threats. While Earth Sinkholes implode in a matter of seconds, Lunar Sinkholes can take minutes, up to hours, to fully finish imploding due to the lower gravity. Because of this, stations caught in the area of a Sinkhole have a chance to not notice that they are descending until it is too late, making rescue harder. \n \n Callers typically report rumbling and cracking noises before the beginning of a sinkhole. Once a sinkhole begins however, callers feel a sensation of sinking, though they typically dismiss.",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 2,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 91,
		"name": "Apollo Muscaria Poisoning",
		"category": Category.BIOLOGICAL,
		"severity": 3,
		"danger": 3,
		"scale": 1,
		"type": Category.BIOLOGICAL,
		"description": "Apollo Muscaria Poisoning refers to the accidental, though sometimes intentional, overdosing on Apollo Muscaria mushrooms, a mushroom that is native to the Moon. While Apollo Muscaria is native to the Moon, and has no natural predators to consume it, both presently and historically, it still possesses hallucinogenic properties. \n \n Like most hallucinogenic substances, though, recreational use is illegal, which does not stop personnel from using it, and leads to situations such as Apollo Muscaria Poisoning due to overuse, since proper serving sizes for the mushrooms are commonly not followed for the purposes of achieving a better high. \n \n The effects of A.M.P, compared to many other poisons or overdose effects, take much longer to set in, often up to 24 to 48 hours before the first effects. In the beginning, it is commonly confused with food poisoning, with throwing up, nausea, and diarrhea being very common. 12 hours later, poison from the Apollo Muscaria which has collected in the nerves due to overuse begins to infiltrate the cells, causing muscle spasms, cramps, sleepwalking, trouble breathing, paralysis, eye twitching, and rarely cardiac arrythmia. The final stage, 4 hours after the last, is when the poison begins to collect in the brain, causing slurring, loss of impulse control, homicidal and suicidal tendencies, depression, mood swings, and, very rarely, total sudden brain death.  ",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 4,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 92,
		"name": "Geminite",
		"category": Category.BIOLOGICAL,
		"severity": 4,
		"danger": 4,
		"scale": 2,
		"type": Category.ANOMALOUS,
		"description": "Geminites are a hostile carbon-based plant-animal alien species that comes to the Moon as a part of their life cycle, and for entertainment. They come to the Moon, and presumably any other low-gravity rocky celestial body (unknown if atmosphere is a deciding factor), such as the Moon, and bury themselves in the ground at the end of their life cycle. Once this is done, the Geminite rapidly decomposes into pollen, the same pollen that is dispersed during a Pollen Burst, and the same pollen that infects personnel during a Pollen Infection. Once the Pollen kills an individual, their biomass is converted into a Geminite. \n \n Geminites take many forms, however, for the sake of brevity, we will only cover the forms used while hunting, as, when a Geminite emerges, that is what they will do in most reported cases, with the other half featuring them leaving the Moon. These forms are; A full humanoid figure with flowers for eyes, a semi-humanoid form with 2 legs leading upwards into a orb shape constructed fully out of grass, a large centipedal form with long antennae used for hunting that are disguised as vines, and a moss like form used to ambush those who walk past it. \n \n Those in the vicinity of a Geminite will often report opened vent covers, clippings of plant matter where they shouldn't be, allergies, and likely a sighting of an unknown figure. ",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 5,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 93,
		"name": "Worker Strike",
		"category": Category.INDUSTRIAL,
		"severity": 2,
		"danger": 2,
		"scale": 4,
		"type": Category.SECURITY,
		"description": "Worker Strikes are a labor related Unauthorized Gathering in which employees of a corporation, or of the Lunar Authority itself, protest against the standards and current practices of their working conditions. Due to being unauthorized, Security Personnel are to shut the strike down, but due to previous incidents of Security Overreach (#94), M.A.R.S Operators must take extra steps to ensure that the information given by the Security Personnel is accurate. In order to do this, the C.R.A.T.E.R's Browser has been equipped with a list of favorited sites commonly used by strikers to plan and organize. \n \n The required tasks of a Worker Strike will be the following, and you must input the proper information in order to submit the report; Organizer,  Location, Size, and Employer or the OLSE.",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 3,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 94,
		"name": "Security Overreach",
		"category": Category.SECURITY,
		"severity": 3,
		"danger": 3,
		"scale": 3,
		"type": Category.SECURITY,
		"description": "Security Overreach refers to any conduct by Security Personnel that violates the Security Code of Conduct in any fashion. In order for an Operator to know when a violation has occurred, a copt of the Security Code of Conduct has been installed into M.A.R.S's C.R.A.T.E.Rs.   ",
