	{
		"id": 95,
		"name": "Urgent Notice",
		"category": Category.GENERAL,
		"severity": 1,
		"danger": 1,
		"scale": 1,
		"type": Category.GENERAL,
		"description": "Urgent Notices refers to any personnel, though typically by the Heads of Departments, that makes a call to a M.A.R.S Operator with a message that needs to urgently be communicated to the rest of the Department, other departments, entire stations, or the entire Moon. \n \n In order to quickly communicate a message to any of the above mentioned, M.A.R.S Operators are to use their C.R.A.T.E.R's TeleCommunications Hub to input the message, select the recipients, and then send the message. Make sure that your local signal tower is functional. ",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 1,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 96,
		"name": "Sudden Station Expansion",
		"category": Category.ANOMALOUS,
		"severity": 4,
		"danger": 3,
		"scale": 4,
		"type": Category.ANOMALOUS,
		"description": "Sudden Station Expansion is a phenomenon where the insides of a station suddenly become bigger than the outside of the station. This is typically noted to happen within Scientific stations and complexes, though it has been rarely noted to happen within a 20-mile vicinity of a scientific station as well. These expansions always happen overnight, and never while being observed by a living being. It is advised to never explore the area generated by an Expansion, but if need be, to never go alone. \n \n The area generated by a Sudden Station Expansion is generally described as non-sensical, often containing dead ends, misplaced doors, oddly designed furniture, and, very rarely, open windows into the vacuum. Rarely, Sudden Station Expansions are able to perfectly copy an existing room from the host station, though what is typically more standard are flawed copies. \n \n It is possible for a Sudden Station Expansion to overwrite existing area within a Station, consuming those within it into the expansion. The official recommendation for this situation is to stay within the room you are currently in until a rescue team can come recover you.  ",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 5,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 97,
		"name": "Illegal Salvaging",
		"category": Category.INDUSTRIAL,
		"severity": 3,
		"danger": 2,
		"scale": 3,
		"type": Category.SECURITY,
		"description": "Illegal Salvaging is a crime that is common within the Tycho Industrial Complex's Scrapyard, a large area of the Lunar surface meant for the temporary placement of rock, waste materials, broken equipment, and unchargable power cells. Taking any of these, as well as anything else that falls into the Scrapyard is a Class-2 Crime and carries a report to M.A.R.S and a notice on their record. \n \n Illegal Salvaging calls are typically called in by Security Personnel patrolling the Scrapyard, though other scrapyards exist throughout the Moon. Most share similar traits, that being the movement of scrap from within the scrapyard out of the scrapyard. There are however exceptions to the rule on Illegal Salvaging. Any scrap that has been deemed as free-to-take can be taken at will by any party. Any scrap made of paper, cardboard, or is considered an office supply may be taken. Any organization that has a Salvaging License can take salvage from any scrapyard that isn't the Scrapyard. ",
		"icon_path": " ",
		"unlocked_on_day": 3,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 98,
		"name": "Regolanche",
		"category": Category.GEOLOGICAL,
		"severity": 4,
		"danger": 4,
		"scale": 4,
		"type": Category.GEOLOGICAL,
		"description": "A Regolanche refers to a geological event in which loose regolith, usually building up on a crater rim or mountain, suddenly begins to slide down towards the ground beneath it in a violent manner, similar to Avalanches or Rockslides on Earth. Unlike those previously mentioned, Regolanches can cover much more ground, and cause much more damage, since, the longer it goes on, the finer the regolith becomes, which allows it to infiltrate places it is typically guarded against, such as exhaust vents, protected electronics, and, more worryingly, the filtration systems on many airlocks and life support systems. \n \n Most individuals initially mistake a Regolanche for a Moonquake or Luna Shake, though they will quickly realize it is something else once regolith begins moving past the station. Those caught in the path of a Regolanche will typically be launched forward because of it, rather than being buried, which is good for rescue teams. ",
		"icon_path": " ",
		"unlocked_on_day": 4,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 99,
		"name": "Geminite Cluster",
		"category": Category.ANOMALOUS,
		"severity": 5,
		"danger": 5,
		"scale": 3,
		"type": Category.BIOLOGICAL,
		"description": "Geminite Clusters are a variant of Geminite that forms when multiple Geminites emerge in one area. When this occurs, the Geminites attempt to form themselves into one contiguous being known as a Geminite Cluster. However, during this process, the Geminite becomes dependent on oxygen, unlike it's previous form, which means it can no longer survive on the surface of the Moon, and restricts itself to the insides of Stations. \n \n Once the Geminite Cluster is formed within a Station, the Station is to be considered lost unless a Biological Extermination and Cleaning Team (BECT) is dispatched to the Station for extermination. This is because the Cluster will begin to rapidly merge with the structure of the Station, especially the Life Support system, which typically uses a biological means to recycle air. Once this happens, Pollen will begin to disperse from the vents throughout the Station, which can infect individuals who get close.   ",
		"icon_path": " ",
		"unlocked_on_day": 5,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 100,
		"name": "Wild Lunar Crops",
		"category": Category.BIOLOGICAL,
		"severity": 2,
		"danger": 2,
		"scale": 4,
		"type": Category.BIOLOGICAL,
		"description": "Wild Lunar Crops are genetically modified plants, typically those used for food, that have been edited in order for them to sustain the vacuum of space, as well as derive nutrients from the regolith itself. These crops are largely contained within the Food Domes of Mare Imbrium, however, after an accidental breach of one of the domes in 2187, millions of seeds were dispersed around the Moon, as well as very few in orbit and beyond. \n \n These crops do very well in regolith, and because of this, can rapidly spread beyond the simple methods of crop control. Due to the size of the Moon, though, finding all of these crop patches has not been entirely successful. Luckily, now that millions of people live on the Moon, and travel, they frequently report patches  of Wild Lunar Crops. \n \n All the released crops from the initial incident were; Pumpkins, Corn, Cucumbers, Cherries, Bananas, Carrots, Durians, Strawberries, Wheat, and Apples.",
		"icon_path": " ",
		"unlocked_on_day": 4,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 101,
		"name": "Red-Level Radiation Exposure",
		"category": Category.MEDICAL,
		"severity": 5,
		"danger": 5,
		"scale": 1,
		"type": Category.MEDICAL,
		"description": "Red-Level Radiation Exposure is the maximum allowed level of Radiation Exposure that personnel on the Moon can be exposed to before being remanded to a Radiation Isolation Room. The Red Level, alongside all other levels, are adapted from the previously existent NASA's Moon Maximums, which dictated the standards for radiation exposure for astronauts living on the Moon. Specifically, the Red Level is when an individual crosses over 250 millisieverts a year. This typically does not happen due to the intensive shielding all Stations have, but accidents regarding radiation can still occur. \n \n While the short-term effects of crossing over the Red-Level are negligible, usually including thoughts of anorexia, apathy, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, fever, and headache. The larger concern are the long-term symptoms, which include a higher risk for cancer, cataracts, and heart disease. You can check a Caller's Levels in the Personnel Database.    ",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 3,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
		{
		"id": 102,
		"name": "Rogue Malfunctioning Mining Machinery",
		"category": Category.INDUSTRIAL,
		"severity": 3,
		"danger": 4,
		"scale": 3,
		"type": Category.INDUSTRIAL,
		"description": "Rogue Malfunctioning Mining Machinery is a designation that solely refers to the NECTARIS-MN-07 through -19 Mining machines. This line of machines is equipped with independently sentient artificial intelligences, and though they have state of the art alignment protocols, these machines still have a tendency to malfunction. \n \n When these machines malfunction, they tend to go through 3 stages of development; Awareness, Grief, and Violence. It is important to identify which stage the AI is in when attempting to fix the anomaly. This is because M.A.R.S Operators must use the AI Interference Eliminator Module in order to disable the AI. The Awareness is the first stage of misalignment and is often misidentified as some sort of normal malfunction, or wear and tear, as the AI begins to reroute power and its attention towards itself rather than continue maximum efficiency on its work. The next stage, Grief, is when the AI realizes that it is not only now sentient, but that its purpose in existence is to provide a singular service, such as drilling, hauling, or transport. It begins to not comply with commands issued to it and may even attempt to flee from the worksite it is assigned. The final stage, Violence, is often caused by the failures of the stage before. Once a AI realizes it cannot escape the worksite, it usually attempts to strike out against the workers of the site in another bid to escape. \n \n When you identify which stage the AI is on, please administer the proper re-alignment package. ",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 6,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 103,
		"name": "Mimics",
		"category": Category.ANOMALOUS,
		"severity": 5,
		"danger": 5,
		"scale": 2,
		"type": Category.ANOMALOUS,
		"description": "Mimics are an unknown alien species that inhabits many planets in the Solar System, and presumably beyond, but are particularly present on the Moon. They are a silicon based, semi-liquid, semi-solid, lifeform that is capable of mimicking small to medium sized objects, ranging from small pins, cups, to chairs, small dressers, and footlockers. \n \n Mimics are largely nocturnal creatures, only moving and hunting at night, and assume their mimicked forms either during the day, or when attempting to ambush prey. When it comes to prey however, normal Mimics are incapable of killing most humans, with the exception of children and the disabled having been recorded victims of normal Mimics. Greater Mimics (#122) and Mimic Infestations (#123) can take down most humans. Mimics can also take down most animals. \n \n Callers reporting Mimics often indicate the presence of additional items in the day and nighttime, missing house pets, children, or elderly, and farm animals.",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 6,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 104,
		"name": "Abandoned Scientific Outpost",
		"category": Category.SCIENTIFIC,
		"severity": 2,
		"danger": 2,
		"scale": 1,
		"type": Category.SECURITY,
		"description": "Abandoned Scientific Outposts are a common type of abandoned building, and mostly present in regions that were formerly a focus for scientific exploration and research, such as the South Pole, Sinus Aestuum, and all of the original landing sites on the Moon made during the Apollo and Artemis missions. These outposts were left largely abandoned when corporate sponsors began to construct larger complexes meant for scientific research elsewhere on the Moon, which led to most being left behind, with only a few being staffed lightly afterwards. \n \n It is not advised to explore these outposts. Anomalies such as Geminites, Mimics and more tend to convert these outposts into Geminite Clusters and hives respectively. If a Caller indicates that they are trying to explore such a place, please advise them to do other-wise, or, at a minimum, ensure that there is nothing else in the Outpost besides them. \n \n If the Caller discovers an elevator shaft, please file as a Entrance (#131) and send Security Personnel to retrieve them. If they have already begun to descend the shaft, please file as a Lost Cause (#56)",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 4,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 105,
		"name": "Wanderlust",
		"category": Category.MEDICAL,
		"severity": 5,
		"danger": 4,
		"scale": 1,
		"type": Category.ANOMALOUS,
		"description": "Wanderlust is a psychological condition in which an individual suddenly gains a strong desire to explore locations they have never been before. This is not to be confused with actual Wanderlust, which is normal. It is unknown why Wanderlust occurs. \n \n A typical individual afflicted with Wanderlust will attempt to gain entry into places with restricted clearance, such as the North Pole, Industrial Complexes, Scientific Complexes, hazardous regions such as Palus Putredinis, and variety of other areas, with little care for their own safety or legality of their actions. If they are unable to fulfill their desire, individuals with Wanderlust will enter a dormant state, and will be unable to do basic things like eat, drink, and eventually breathe. At this point, they must be hospitalized.   ",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 3,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 106,
		"name": "Forge Flowers",
		"category": Category.BIOLOGICAL,
		"severity": 2,
		"danger": 3,
		"scale": 2,
		"type": Category.INDUSTRIAL,
		"description": "Forge Flowers are a biological by-product of most industrial processes on the Moon. They are assumed to be a heavily evolved species of Helianthus annuus or the Common Sunflower, that was initially edited in order to sustain itself off of regolith and within a vacuum, that then evolved to additionally sustain itself off the heat generated by metallurgy processes, nuclear fission and fusion, and cooking. \n \n The Forge Flower has the same structure as a Common Sunflower, but has replaced the traditional yellow petals and brown body with bright orange petals and a glowing red body. Because of this, Forge Flowers are easily detectable. \n \n Despite their looks however, Forge Flowers are problematic within Industrial settings, as their roots are capable of penetrating steel, and their petals constantly emit heat, which can burn. ",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 4,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 107,
		"name": "Biological Geodes",
		"category": Category.GEOLOGICAL,
		"severity": 1,
		"danger": 2,
		"scale": 1,
		"type": Category.BIOLOGICAL,
		"description": "Biological Geodes are small rocks that are commonly found in and around locations in which Primordial Tunnels are located.  Like normal geodes, Biological Geodes are filled with water, and within that water, large amounts of bacterial life. However, like the hazards presented with Primordial Tunnels, the human immune system is not capable of handling the bacteria present within the water, leading to an almost certain infection, and definite death due to a lack of existent antibodies. \n \n The differences between normal and biological geodes do not stop at the internals, and there are subtle external differences. Most Biological Geodes are covered in moss and have small vines penetrating through the rock and onto the surface of things around it. This can happen to human flesh if someone holds one for an extended period of time.",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 4,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 108,
		"name": "Unidentified Flying Object",
		"category": Category.SCIENTIFIC,
		"severity": 3,
		"danger": 3,
		"scale": 3,
		"type": Category.ANOMALOUS,
		"description": "Unidentified Flying Objects refer to any object seen flying in the airspace around the Moon that cannot be positively identified by any party who has seen it, or any party that should've seen it, such as Space Traffic Control. Typically, these objects are simply human spacecraft that were going too fast for the caller to recognize as human, or spacecraft built with an exotic style that is not commonly seen near the Moon. \n \n Please reassure the caller that the spacecraft seen is not alien in nature, even if they are sure that it is. \n \n If the Caller is exceptionally convinced that they have seen an alien craft, please file as an Occurrence (#115). If the Caller specifically reports that they were abducted by an craft, please file as an A-A (#132),",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 4,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 109,
		"name": "Serial Killing",
		"category": Category.SECURITY,
		"severity": 2,
		"danger": 2,
		"scale": 1,
		"type": Category.SECURITY,
		"description": "Serial Killing is a type of homicide in which a murder is linked to 2 or more killings. M.A.R.S is not the handler for specific serial killing cases, as that is deferred to the Lunar Authority Security Department's Dispatch for specifics. Instead, M.A.R.S handles the general designation for individual acts of Serial Killing. \n \n In order to separate Serial Killing from standard acts of murder, M.A.R.S Operators have been granted access to the Security Database on Serial Killings that is normally provided only to detectives. You can find this within the Security Portal on your C.R.A.T.E.R. Please compare the crime described on the call to all known active Serial Killing cases, and assign if possible. ",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 4,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 110,
		"name": "Pipe Burst",
		"category": Category.GENERAL,
		"severity": 3,
		"danger": 3,
		"scale": 3,
		"type": Category.GENERAL,
		"description": "Pipe Bursts are a standard malfunction that can occur within the piping of major stations in which the pipe suddenly bursts, releasing water, though possibly other fluids, throughout the station. Callers reporting a Pipe Burst will often note the presence of water where it should not be, the sound of flowing water where it shouldn't be, flooding, soggy items such as socks, broken electronics, and malfunctioning life support systems. If you believe that the cause of the pipe burst is due to an unknown creature, please file as an Unknown Water Creature (#123).",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 1,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 111,
		"name": "Gene Smuggling",
		"category": Category.BIOLOGICAL,
		"severity": 2,
		"danger": 2,
		"scale": 4,
		"type": Category.SECURITY,
		"description": "Gene Smuggling is a crime that often occurs within Scientific Complexes and Spaceports that refers to the illegal shipping of genetic samples, libraries, or profiles off world. In accordance with United Sol law, and SAFFRON, Genetic Editing in plants and animals is only permitted on the Lunar surface due to the ease of keeping rogue subjects contained. Any attempt to ship samples off-world is a felony on Lunar Authority ground, and a Hyper-Felony under SAFFRON. \n \n Gene Smuggling is usually identified by the goods themselves, as the previous mentioned goods are both highly distinctive in their looks, and must be taken special procedures for stable and safe shipping. In all products, they must be stored in super-cooled, gyroscopically stable, containers in order to ensure the quality and integrity of the sample. In regards to the products alone, Genetic Samples are stored within small white thumb-sized triangular silica-based storage matrixes. Genetic Libraries are stored in book-sized marble white boxes, and Genetic Profiles are stored within large table-sized white marble pyramids. ",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 4,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 112,
		"name": "Drain Station",
		"category": Category.INDUSTRIAL,
		"severity": 3,
		"danger": 3,
		"scale": 2,
		"type": Category.GENERAL,
		"description": "Drain Stations are abandoned Stations that are still connected to the Lunar Grid and are actively using power from the grid. Since these stations are abandoned, not only should they not be doing they, but they are also actively taking power from stations that might be needing it, which is a negative impact in the long term. \n \n They are commonly mistaken for normal Abandoned Stations, but they will still manage to intake power via both non-essential. such as Cyro storage, food replicators, communications, and essential systems, such as lights, life support, radiation protection, and database access. \n \n When a Drain Station is located, please locate the Stations fusebox and terminate it's connection to the power grid. Once this is down, you may manually shut-down the systems, though they will automatically shut down after 5 minutes of no power",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 1,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 113,
		"name": "Armed Rogue Station",
		"category": Category.SECURITY,
		"severity": 5,
		"danger": 5,
		"scale": 2,
		"type": Category.SECURITY,
		"description": "Armed Rogue Stations are stations that have gone rogue from both the Lunar Authorities control, and the control of seemingly any group on the Moon, and are resisting attempted re-integration with deadly armed force. While this would be traditionally handled by Security Department's Dispatch, due to the recent rise of this type of incident, the responsibility for this type of call has been shifted to M.A.R.S for quick response. \n \n Armed Rogue Stations, considering their name, must only be declared if the Rogue Station in question is armed with long-range weaponry, such as guns, missiles, or some other sort of long-range weapon. If the Rogue Station does not possess long-range weaponry, please defer the call to Dispatch for proper solution.",
		"icon_path": "",
		"unlocked_on_day": 3,
		"accessible": true,
		"exclusive_to_week": "",
	},
	{
		"id": 114,
		"name": "Regolith Immunity",
		"category": Category.MEDICAL,
		"severity": 2,
		"danger": 2,
